KG42.register("clusters-eced85c26946d7c57b80926a",{"id":"38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v142-d-K002","paper":"38-bidirectional_ev_trading","label":"EV surplus energy sale permission, type restrictions, and net trading representation","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K002","label":"EV surplus energy sale permission, type restrictions, and net trading representation","market_meaning":"When a customer owns sellable EV storage, electricity sale to the aggregator is represented by the negative value of net energy consumption; Type III permission is limited to connected charging intervals, while Type I/II retain the branch prohibiting electricity sale. Customer 1's sale upper limit is only a specified example; when optimal linear billing is adopted, the corresponding net energy bill can be connected.","mechanism_ids":["M01"],"market_types":["DEM","LEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","activation","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"conditional","scope_explanation":"Product semantics and execution capability reference the same M01 customer-aggregator electricity sale definition. EV type, connected interval, and Customer 1 example are retained separately; the shared settlement interface is enabled only when optimal linear billing applies. LEM and DEM are the original classifications of the frozen Rule-Chain; this assembly does not on that basis determine that the two market types are equivalent or that cross-market trading exists.","assembly_status":"assembled","boundary_rationale":"This cluster expresses independent electricity sale permission and signed transaction volume; the boundary stops at capability and representation, and does not claim that battery physical dispatch has already been completed. The linear settlement Rule-Chain is shared only as a conditional interface, and its primary ownership still belongs to the collaborative scheduling settlement cluster.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide electricity sale permission differentiated by EV type, the prohibition branch, and the Customer 1 example upper limit."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R006","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Provide the product semantics of sellable surplus energy, and the convention that negative net energy represents electricity sale."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R005","ownership":"shared","role":"interface","rationale":"Only when the optimal linear billing condition holds, provide a billing interface for the optimal net energy corresponding to electricity sale, and do not duplicate ownership of settlement rules here."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g02-e28","v141-b-g03-E03"],"rationale":"The general surplus energy sale permission and sign convention are supplemented by EV type restrictions and the boundary of a specific example; different conditional branches do not substitute for one another, and the example upper limit is not extrapolated as a universal standard."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K002-L02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::x_total","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R005::x::v141-c-R005-x-i-tot-star","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14"],"rationale":"The same signed net energy becomes the linear billing quantity in the optimal dispatch instance; the bill is connected only when feasibility and that billing scheme are satisfied, and the general transaction quantity and the optimal instance are not declared to be unconditionally identical objects."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K002-M01","kind":"same_quantity","member_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::x_total","v141-c-R006::x::v141-c-R006-x001"],"canonical_ref":null,"display_policy":"linked_distinct","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E02","v141-b-g01-E03"],"rationale":"The common system definition indicates that both are customer time-period net energy including appliances and EV, and negative values both represent electricity sale; retain the different local roles in product representation and transaction execution, and do not mistake it for total battery discharge."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G01","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"R006 is labeled LEM, while R004 and the shared R005 are labeled DEM, but the corresponding quotations do not give geographical local or feeder market boundaries. The common transaction semantics can be assembled, but the market classification identity remains undetermined.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R006::V::product.local_energy","v141-c-R004::V::execution.energy_trade"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g02-e28"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Manual verification should determine the market classification and the applicable boundary of the product node; in the meantime retain the two original labels DEM and LEM, and do not derive additional trading paths."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G02","category":"upstream_missing","description":"Permission, sign, and type lower bound do not constitute complete battery execution constraints; the connected interval, available storage, and battery state limits still have no complete condition Rule-Chain citable by this cluster. A negative allowed lower bound also does not mean that electricity sale necessarily occurs for the customer.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::theta::theta_xmin_tot","v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g01-E04","v141-b-g01-E05","v141-b-g01-E06","v141-b-g02-e28"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"If extended to executable electricity sale rules, upstream supplements the interval and battery feasibility Rule-Chain; the current candidate continues to be limited to permission and net quantity representation."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G03","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The quotation for the Customer 1 example includes Type I in the wording of a discharge-capable setup, which is a point to be verified against the EV type definition. Currently only the Type III electricity sale upper limit explicitly given there is retained, and the general type conditions are not rewritten on that basis.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::theta::theta_xmin_tot_c1","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e28","v141-b-g03-E03"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Trace back to the original example and type definitions, confirm the wording and applicable scenario; keep the example attribute of the Customer 1 upper limit."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K002-G04","category":"unverified_source","description":"The electricity sale definition, type conditions, example upper limit, and shared billing basis all come from B material that has not been independently audited; assembled only means that the stated permission candidate has formed a semantic combination.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004","v141-c-R005","v141-c-R006"],"object_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-E03","v141-b-g02-e28","v141-b-g03-E03","v141-b-g01-E13","v141-b-g01-E14"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Subsequently check the original source, maintain source_status and the experimental candidate nature, and do not treat the assembly status as scientific confirmation."}]},"rule_refs":["38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v141-c-R004","38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v141-c-R006","38-bidirectional_ev_trading::v141-c-R005"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-54652b41fe65fa28","COMP-76d88cced26fe0a5","COMP-9d4b5e6b1dce6608","COMP-ee664d90be53dd00","KG40-88d16cf517d0bffb"]});
